sisa-attention
==============

This package contains original code. No third-party source code is copied
into it. Several published methods shaped its design, and they are credited
below. The license terms named here are those of the respective reference
implementations; they are listed for attribution only.


Methods
-------

Forget gate (FoX)
    The additive forget-gate term F_i - F_j, with F the cumulative sum of
    log sigmoid(z), follows the Forgetting Transformer, and the structure of
    its backward pass follows the scheme of the reference FoX implementation
    (MIT License).
    Paper: "Forgetting Transformer: Softmax Attention with a Forget Gate"
    (ICLR 2025).

Chunked state-space decomposition (Mamba-2 SSD)
    The exact chunk-factored evaluation of the decay exp(g_i - g_j) as
    row factor x per-tile scalar x column factor follows the chunked
    structured state-space duality (SSD) algorithm of Mamba-2. Its reference
    implementation is distributed under the Apache License 2.0.
    Paper: "Transformers are SSMs: Generalized Models and Efficient Algorithms
    Through Structured State Space Duality" (ICML 2024).

Data-dependent rotation (Mamba-3)
    The rotation of C and B by the cumulative data-dependent phase
    Phi_t = sum of theta_tau (the rotary form of a complex-valued state
    update) follows Mamba-3. Its reference implementation (mamba_ssm) is
    distributed under the Apache License 2.0.
    Paper: "Mamba-3: Improved Sequence Modeling using State Space Principles"
    (ICLR 2026).

FlashAttention-style tiling
    The online-softmax forward kernel and the split of the backward pass into
    a dq kernel and a dk/dv kernel follow FlashAttention-2.
    Papers: "FlashAttention: Fast and Memory-Efficient Exact Attention with
    IO-Awareness" (NeurIPS 2022) and "FlashAttention-2: Faster Attention with
    Better Parallelism and Work Partitioning" (ICLR 2024).

Chunked linear cross-entropy (optional kernel)
    The optional fused LM-head cross-entropy in sisa.kernels.linear_ce, which
    processes the vocabulary chunk by chunk and never materializes the full
    logits tensor, follows the approach of Liger Kernel (BSD 2-Clause License).
    Paper: "Liger Kernel: Efficient Triton Kernels for LLM Training" (2024).


Software
--------

PyTorch and Triton are runtime dependencies and are not redistributed.

The examples can optionally use the GPT-NeoX-20B tokenizer through the
`tokenizers` library; it is downloaded at run time and is not redistributed.
Paper: "GPT-NeoX-20B: An Open-Source Autoregressive Language Model"
(2022).
